{"id": "s11-ny-practice-2", "title": "Practice 2: -ный, -ной, -ский", "blocks": [{"t": "note", "text": "Sentences and their English: Tatoeba (tatoeba.org, CC BY 2.0 FR). Words, meanings and how each word is built: the English Wiktionary (CC BY-SA 4.0)."}], "exercises": [{"type": "fill", "q": "слы́шать → ___", "answers": ["слышный", "слы́шный"], "hint": "the adjective in -ный", "why": "**слы́шный** — audible (able to be heard). Wiktionary: слы́шать + -ный.", "id": "q1"}, {"type": "fill", "q": "наро́д → ___", "answers": ["народный", "наро́дный"], "hint": "the adjective in -ный", "why": "**наро́дный** — people's. Wiktionary: наро́д + -ный.", "id": "q2"}, {"type": "match", "q": "Match each word with its meaning (Wiktionary's definitions).", "pairs": [["све́тский", "(relational) society, high-society"], ["ви́дный", "visible, conspicuous"], ["слы́шный", "audible (able to be heard)"], ["наро́дный", "people's"]], "why": "From Wiktionary: све́тский — (relational) society, high-society; ви́дный — visible, conspicuous; слы́шный — audible (able to be heard); наро́дный — people's.", "id": "q3"}, {"type": "fill", "q": "ум → ___", "answers": ["умный", "у́мный"], "hint": "the adjective in -ный", "why": "**у́мный** — clever, smart, intelligent. Wiktionary: ум + -ный.", "id": "q4"}, {"type": "fill", "q": "часть → ___", "answers": ["частный", "ча́стный"], "hint": "the adjective in -ный", "why": "**ча́стный** — private. Wiktionary: часть + -ный.", "id": "q5"}, {"type": "fill", "q": "ве́ра → ___", "answers": ["верный", "ве́рный"], "hint": "the adjective in -ный", "why": "**ве́рный** — true, faithful, loyal. Wiktionary: ве́ра + -ный.", "id": "q6"}, {"type": "fill", "q": "труд → ___", "answers": ["трудный", "тру́дный"], "hint": "the adjective in -ный", "why": "**тру́дный** — hard, difficult. Wiktionary: труд + -ный.", "id": "q7"}, {"type": "match", "q": "Match each word with its meaning (Wiktionary's definitions).", "pairs": [["у́мный", "clever, smart, intelligent"], ["ча́стный", "private"], ["ве́рный", "true, faithful, loyal"], ["тру́дный", "hard, difficult"]], "why": "From Wiktionary: у́мный — clever, smart, intelligent; ча́стный — private; ве́рный — true, faithful, loyal; тру́дный — hard, difficult.", "id": "q8"}, {"type": "fill", "q": "звук → ___", "answers": ["звучный", "зву́чный"], "hint": "the adjective in -ный", "why": "**зву́чный** — resounding, sonorous. Wiktionary: звук + -ный.", "id": "q9"}, {"type": "fill", "q": "извести́ть → ___", "answers": ["известный", "изве́стный"], "hint": "the adjective in -ный", "why": "**изве́стный** — known, familiar. Wiktionary: извести́ть + -ный.", "id": "q10"}, {"type": "fill", "q": "нау́ка → ___", "answers": ["научный", "нау́чный"], "hint": "the adjective in -ный", "why": "**нау́чный** — scientific. Wiktionary: нау́ка + -ный.", "id": "q11"}, {"type": "fill", "q": "поря́док → ___", "answers": ["порядочный", "поря́дочный"], "hint": "the adjective in -ный", "why": "**поря́дочный** — decent, honest, respectable. Wiktionary: поря́док + -ный.", "id": "q12"}]}